   ships a NOTICE file of its own.

   `nm` is pulled in by the Linux implementation of `connectivity_plus` only;
   the Android and Windows builds of this application do not contain it. It is
   used unmodified, so the Mozilla Public License obligations reach only the
   unmodified upstream files.

   `tray_manager` 0.8.0 talks to the operating system through `nativeapi`,
   `nativeapi_flutter` and `cnativeapi` (all MIT, same author as
   `tray_manager`; the MIT text is reproduced above). `cnativeapi` carries the
   C sources of the native tray library, which are compiled into the Windows
   and Android artifacts at build time; they are used unmodified. The
   migration dropped `menu_base` and `shortid`, which only the removed
   legacy API needed, and moved `objective_c` and `record_use` forward — both
   serve the macOS port, which this repository does not build. `ffi` was
   already in the graph and became a direct dependency for the Win32 wrappers
   (mutex, Job Object).

   Platform components used at runtime: the Android VpnService API
   (Apache License 2.0, part of the Android Open Source Project) and the
   Windows proxy settings through WinINet and the registry (no third-party
   code is redistributed).

